pywhat/Data/mac_vendors.json
----------------------------
MAC address prefixes (MA-L, MA-M, MA-S and IAB) and the organisations they are assigned to, as
registered with the IEEE Registration Authority
(https://standards.ieee.org/products-programs/regauth/). Added in 2021 (commit e589732). The
list it was copied from is not recorded.

Licence: not recorded.


pywhat/Data/phone_codes.json
----------------------------
Country calling codes (ITU-T E.164) and their countries. 226 of the 228 entries are those of
the GitHub gist "CountryCodes.json" by anubhavshrimal (2016,
https://gist.github.com/anubhavshrimal/75f6183458db8c453306f93521e93d37), a fork of the gist
"Country and Dial or Phone codes in JSON format" by Goles (2012,
https://gist.github.com/Goles/3196253). Added in 2021 (commits 71cdefb and f1c993d).

Licence: not recorded; neither gist states one.


Regexes in pywhat/Data/regex.json
---------------------------------
Five regexes are based on entries of the regex101 community library
(https://regex101.com/library), rewritten for pyWhat in #276. regex101 states no licence for
library entries.
  Browser User Agent            "Parsing browser User Agents" by OnlineCop
                                https://regex101.com/r/aL8lD7/2
  Regex101 Permalink            "regex101.com permalink id grabber" by chris mccoy
                                https://regex101.com/r/wY0rM7/3
  ISO 8601 Timestamp            "RFC3339 DateTime" (no author given)
                                https://regex101.com/r/qH0sU7/1
  United Kingdom (UK) Postcode  "UK Postcode Checker" by MaffooBristol
                                https://regex101.com/r/tH9mQ1/1
  Cron Schedule                 "Cron schedule" (no author given)
                                https://regex101.com/r/vY5eL1/1

Some of the bug bounty regexes and their "Exploit" texts are based on the regex database of
Dora (https://github.com/sdushantha/dora, #146):
  Copyright (c) 2021 Siddharth Dushantha, under the MIT License.
Dora's README says that many of its regexes were taken from truffleHogRegexes (GPL-3.0),
secretx (GPL-3.0), gitGraber, shhgit, w13scan, SecretFinder, nuclei-templates,
AdvancedKeyHacks, pentest-tools, gitleaks and dalfox, and most of its exploitation methods from
keyhacks (https://github.com/streaak/keyhacks). More "Exploit" texts were written from
keyhacks' README in #162. keyhacks states no licence.

Some regexes are based on the patterns of gf (https://github.com/tomnomnom/gf):
  Copyright (c) 2018 Tom Hudson, under the MIT License.
Three are based on patterns proposed in pull requests to gf (#273): IPv4 CIDR Block (#25 by
nikitastupin), Log4Shell (Log4j JNDI Lookup) Payload (#61 by jreisinger) and Tox ID (#84 by
johndoe-sh).

The Uniform Resource Locator (URL) regex contains the list of top-level domains that IANA
publishes (https://data.iana.org/TLD/tlds-alpha-by-domain.txt, fetched by
scripts/get_tlds.py). IANA states no licence for this list.

